---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import '../styles/download.css';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Hunter-124/Chudware';
const LATEST = `${REPO}/releases/latest`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Download Chudware" description="Download the free, open-source Chudware desktop app for Windows, Linux, and macOS from GitHub Releases, or build it from source.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Desktop app</p>
      <h1>Download Chudware.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Free, open-source builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS, published on GitHub Releases. No account, no license key.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="panel dl-primary">
        <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="download" /></span>
        <div class="dl-primary-body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Latest release</p>
          <h2>Chudware desktop</h2>
          <p class="dl-note">The latest GitHub release lists every installer and package it ships. Pick the file for your platform using the guide below.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button" href={LATEST}>Download from GitHub</a>
      </article>

      {/* Filenames follow packaging/artifact_names.py, the single source of truth
          for release asset names. */}
      <div class="dl-grid">
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="windows" /></span>
            <h3>Windows</h3>
          </header>
          <p>x86-64 installers: an interactive setup program and an MSI package.</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>Setup (.exe)</span><span>Chudware-Setup-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.exe</span><span class="dl-build-note">For an ordinary interactive install.</span></li>
            <li><span>Installer (.msi)</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.msi</span><span class="dl-build-note">For managed and scripted deployment — Group Policy, Intune, msiexec.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href={LATEST}>Download for Windows <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="linux" /></span>
            <h3>Linux</h3>
          </header>
          <p>x86-64 builds as an AppImage, distribution packages, and a plain archive.</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>AppImage</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-linux-x86_64.AppImage</span></li>
            <li><span>.deb</span><span>chudware_&lt;version&gt;_amd64.deb</span></li>
            <li><span>.rpm</span><span>chudware-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;release&gt;.x86_64.rpm</span></li>
            <li><span>.tar.zst</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-linux-x86_64.tar.zst</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href={LATEST}>Download for Linux <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="apple" /></span>
            <h3>macOS</h3>
          </header>
          <p>x86-64 zip archive. Runs on Intel Macs, and on Apple silicon through Rosetta 2.</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>App (.zip)</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-macos-x86_64.zip</span><span class="dl-build-note">Unpack it and drag Chudware into Applications.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href={LATEST}>Download for macOS <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="supporting-copy dl-sysnote">All desktop builds are 64-bit and need a GPU driver with hardware-accelerated 3D. Without one the app won't start. Not every release carries every format; the release's asset list is authoritative.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-linux-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Linux packages</p>
        <h2 id="dl-linux-title">Pick the format that fits your distribution.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each format carries the same application. Distribution packages integrate with your package manager; the AppImage and archive run without installing anything.</p>
      </header>
      <dl class="dl-formats">
        <div><dt><Icon name="package" /> .deb</dt><dd>For Debian and Ubuntu. Install with <code>sudo apt install ./chudware_&lt;version&gt;_amd64.deb</code>; removes cleanly with apt.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="package" /> .rpm</dt><dd>For Fedora, RHEL, and openSUSE. Install with <code>sudo dnf install ./chudware-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;release&gt;.x86_64.rpm</code> or zypper.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="download" /> AppImage</dt><dd>One portable file with nothing to install. Mark it executable with <code>chmod +x</code> and run it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="archive" /> .tar.zst</dt><dd>Plain archive for any distribution; unpack and run from anywhere.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-verify-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Verify and update</p>
        <h2 id="dl-verify-title">Check the file before you run it.</h2>
        <p class="lede">GitHub shows a SHA-256 digest beside each release asset. Compare it with <code>sha256sum</code> on Linux, <code>shasum -a 256</code> on macOS, or <code>Get-FileHash</code> in PowerShell.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">In-app updates</p>
        <p>The desktop app checks the latest GitHub release for a signed update manifest. A downloaded update must match the manifest's size and SHA-256 digest and carry a valid Ed25519 signature from the Chudware release key before the app stages it for installation.</p>
        <p>Only download Chudware from the project's GitHub releases or build it yourself from source.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-source-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Build from source</p>
        <h2 id="dl-source-title">Or build it yourself.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Chudware is open source under the MIT License. The repository README covers the toolchain, dependencies, and build commands for each platform.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Source code</p>
        <p>The C++ application, the Python engine services, the packaging scripts, and the release workflows are all in one public repository.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${REPO}#building-from-source`}>Building from source <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
      <h2>Install it, then build your first part.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The install guides walk through each platform; the first-part guide takes it from there.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={LATEST}>Download from GitHub</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/">Read the install guides</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
